ing to further education. A's strengths: anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: unfriendly, not open to new ideas, unhealthy eating, unorganized.\n\nWhich candidate best fits criteria? Reliability: C (100% reliable), B (very conscientious), D (responsibility), A unknown. Stress resilience: B handles stress well, D responds adequately, C unknown but quick decisions maybe implies calm, A unknown. Technical competence: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, spatial vision; B good at weather, computer; C quick decisions, attention; D problem solving. Decision quality: C quick correct decisions, D solves problems extremely well, B good weather assessment, A leadership. Attention: C excellent attention, D concentration, B memory issue. Cooperation: C positive atmosphere, B nasty remarks, D loner/moody, A unfriendly. Communication: C difficulty communicating, B nasty remarks, D arrogant, A unfriendly. Responsibility: D takes responsibility seriously, B conscientious, C reliable, A leadership.\n\nOverall, C seems strong on reliability, attention, decision, crew atmosphere. The concerns are communication and egocentric, and lack of willingness for further education. Those are important but perhaps less safety-critical than memory issue (B) or weak leadership (D). So C may be best.\n\nThus I might shift my vote to C, aligning with Agent 1. Provide reasoning: C's core safety criteria outweigh concerns. Also note that D's leadership weakness and moody traits could impair crew cooperation more than C's communication difficulty. So I will change my vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 1's points and maybe Agent 2's concerns. Provide explicit facts: 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention, quick correct decisions. Also mention concerns: difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I now support Candidate C...\" etc.\n\nNow meta